        <mxCell id="kZwhHGzqvlMfPyiFF4_c-26" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Learning:&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Keep Follow as a different table, instead of maintaining FollowerUserID[] in User table.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Why?&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;1. It allows us to track date at which two users started following each other etc&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;2. In order to check all followers of a given user, I can simply query this table instead of querying the cumbersome User table&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
